text:
The trait is a belief that certain truths and principles are universal and unchanging, which is a mix of certainty, immutability and truth. No single head names that whole bundle. Stability (150) names unchangeability, but it describes things that don't change, not a doctrinal position. Certainty (474) is nearer to dogmatic conviction, but the trait is about the universality of the principles, not about how sure the believer is.

Of the candidates, none fits well. Stability fits "unchanging" only, and Truth fits "truths" only.

{"reason": "Absolutism bundles universal truth, immutability and exceptionless application, and no single listed head names that whole combination.", "head": "none"}

