text:
The trait is a refusal to admit one's own fault and a habit of blaming others. Head 947 (Guilt) covers being at fault, but it names guilt itself, not the evasion of it. Head 155 (Attribution) covers ascribing a cause, which is close to assigning blame, but it is neutral and has no moral sense of dodging responsibility. No head names denial of one's own part, so none is a true home.

Attribution is the nearest fit in meaning, since blame-shifting is attributing the cause elsewhere. Even so, the trait is a moral failing of self-exculpation, and the thesaurus has no head for that among these.

{"reason": "No listed head names refusing to own one's fault; Guilt is the state of being at fault and Attribution is neutral cause-ascription, so neither is the trait's home.", "head": "none"}

