text:
The trait "extreme", said of a person, most naturally means going to excess or being immoderate. Among the listed heads, Exaggeration (extravagant, overwrought) comes closest, though it is about statement rather than conduct. Severity covers harshness, which is a different quality, and Edge is spatial. Roget's head for this quality would be Excess or Violence, and neither is listed, so Exaggeration is only a partial fit.

Exaggeration names overstating, not extremeness in character, so it is not a clean match. "Extravagant" and "overwrought" do overlap with extreme, but the head's core is communication, so I judge it not the home.

{"reason": "Exaggeration concerns overstatement in communication, not extremeness as a personal quality, and no other listed head fits better.", "head": "none"}

