text:
The trait is an orientation toward the future, with an emphasis on what is new and emerging. Head 121 (Futurity) names the future itself, a time relation rather than a personal quality. Head 510 (Foresight) is about anticipating and planning, which is close to "forward-thinking", but it does not cover the emphasis on technology and novelty. Head 123 (Newness) covers novelty only. "Futuristic" in the sense of featuring future-oriented trends best fits Futurity, whose adjectives are "future" and "to come", though that is a loose fit.

Foresight describes a person who looks ahead, whereas "futuristic" describes something that belongs to or resembles the future. The description stresses emerging trends and future possibilities, so Futurity is the nearest head.

