The trait is broad knowledge across many fields, and the nearest head is Learning (539), whose words (erudition, scholarship, attainment) name wide knowledge. Generality (78) is about the general as opposed to the particular, not a person's knowledge. Scholar (492) names a learned person, but not breadth in particular.

