text:
The IPIP-NEO "Liberalism" facet (under Openness) measures readiness to challenge authority and tradition, i.e. a liberal political and social outlook. Head 942 holds "liberalism" only in the sense of generosity, and 816 is about giving freely. Head 737b (Politics) covers ideology and partisanship but is not specifically liberal attitudes. Head 748 (Freedom) is about liberty, not an open-minded outlook. Head 740 (Lenity) names tolerance, which is close, but it is mainly about mildness in treatment. The nearest fit is Politics, since the trait is a political-ideological orientation, though the match is loose.

The facet is a bundle of attitudes (open to change, challenging authority), and no head names the whole of it. Politics names ideology generally, not a liberal one. I judge that none is a true home.

{"reason": "The trait is a liberal, change-seeking, authority-questioning outlook, while 'liberalism' in 942 means generosity and the other heads cover only parts or a different topic.", "head": "none"}

