The trait is a view about free will: choices are not determined by prior causes and the person could have done otherwise. Head 748, Freedom, is about social liberty and independence, and 609, Choice, is about selecting and options, which is nearer in topic. Roget's Thesaurus has a separate head, Necessity (601), for determinism, and Freedom in the sense of free will is not in this list. Head 609 names choosing, not the doctrine that choice is uncaused, so it is only a shared topic. Head 748 includes "independence" and "free", but it means freedom from restraint. The closest is arguably 748, but it is a different sense.

Freedom of the will is not what 748 names, so I answer none.

{"reason": "No listed head names the doctrine of uncaused free will; Freedom (748) is social liberty and Choice (609) is mere selection.", "head": "none"}

